N = 24, T=5 R=3 P=1 S=0, 400 ticks; average payoff = score / games

cooperate vs defect      defect 3.03, cooperate 1.48
tit-for-tat vs cooperate TFT 3.00, cooperate 3.00
tit-for-tat vs defect
  tick       defect      TFT
  5            2.33     1.87
  20           2.40     1.63
  100          1.48     1.83
  400          1.12     1.95

all six strategies together, tick 400
  unforgiving      2.67
  tit-for-tat      2.51
  defect           2.89
  unknown          2.23
  random           2.28
  cooperate        2.24

One honest difference from NetLogo: there, agents wander a 441-patch world
and meet sparsely, so opponents recur rarely. Here everyone is paired
every tick out of 24, so each pair meets roughly every 23 ticks and the
retaliatory strategies get enough encounters to learn. The two
implementations are answering slightly different questions.
